From 024cc841c3b4958dc0a5f6a340aaa2144342960f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:21:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [zigbee] OTA: delta images

A delta (sub-element 0xF101) is an esp_delta_ota patch (detools,
heatshrink) against the image the device runs, behind a 64-byte header
with the magic and that image's validation hash; a device running
another image refuses it at the first block. The patch output goes
through the same OTA backend, so signature and downgrade checks still
apply.

Every build keeps its image as .esphome/zigbee_ota/<name>/<VERSION>.bin.
With `delta_base:` (a kept file version or a .bin path) the build also
writes firmware.zigbee.delta.ota, which the dashboard offers next to the
full file. A one-line change came to ~10 KB, 2 % of the full file.
Making a delta needs detools in ESPHome's Python; the device side adds
the espressif/esp_delta_ota component.

Idea and format from github.com/jabla/esphome-hiflow-zigbee.

